# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Seam edges (mitcad#1773) on seam-edges.json: the view draws the edges
# where the shape changes and leaves out the seams where a round face
# closes on itself smoothly.
#   - The box with a hole (F1.b0): its 12 edges and the hole's two
#     circles; the hole's seam left out.
#   - The cylinder (F5.b0): its two circles; its seam left out.
#   - The plate with rounded corners (F6.b0): all 24 edges, the roundings'
#     tangent boundaries too; nothing left out.
#   - The teardrop (F9.b0): its two splines and the crease at its tip;
#     nothing left out.
# Sweeps whose side face comes in pieces (mitcad#2148): the edge between
# two pieces is drawn where they are different analytic surfaces.
#   - Along a line and a tangent arc (F12.b0): the caps' circles and the
#     circle between the cylinder and the torus; the cylinder's and the
#     torus's seams left out.
#   - Along a line, an arc and a line (F15.b0): the caps' circles and both
#     circles between the pieces; the three seams left out.
#   - Along two arcs of one circle (F18.b0): the caps' circles only; the
#     circle between the torus's two pieces and their seams left out.
#   - The line-and-arc sweep mirrored and joined (F21.b0, GitHub issue
#     516): the caps' circles and the circle between the cylinder and each
#     torus, on the original and on the copy; the seams left out.
# Faces split into pieces on one surface: no line between the pieces.
#   - The ball (F23.b0): its two poles (degenerated edges, drawn as
#     before); its seam and the circle between its pieces left out.
#   - The torus (F25.b0): nothing; its seams (the one round the tube
#     whole, the one round the axis cut in two by the split) and the two
#     circles between its pieces left out.
# Run by tools/ui-seam-edges-test.sh.
expect-ever 'View area'
wait-idle

expect-view-seams F1.b0 14 1
expect-view-seams F5.b0 2 1
expect-view-seams F6.b0 24 0
expect-view-seams F9.b0 3 0
expect-view-seams F12.b0 3 2
expect-view-seams F15.b0 4 3
expect-view-seams F18.b0 2 3
expect-view-seams F21.b0 4 3
expect-view-seams F23.b0 2 2
expect-view-seams F25.b0 0 5
